Upstream project
----------------
Hardware design, shield schematic, assembly documentation and the
pre-configured MCUXpresso project come from the NXP Line Follower project:

    https://gitfront.io/r/cristiannxp/xHvo63TFm7h4/NXP-Linefollower/

Its licensing, as stated by that project:

    Hardware (PCB, schematics, CAD)   CERN-OHL-S-2.0
    Documentation (markdown, images)  CC BY-SA 4.0
    Software (firmware, examples)     MIT

Material in this repository derived from it:

  * source/hbridge.c, include/hbridge.h
        Adapted from the upstream source/hbridge.c and include/hbridge.h.
        Behaviour on the motors is unchanged. Differences: an unused local
        removed, a self-assignment in HbridgeInit() dropped, motors explicitly
        stopped at init, and the DRV8833 duty-cycle rule documented.

  * source/robot.c (sensors_read, sensors_raw)
        The per-sensor GPIO reads and the bit packing (bit 0 = S10 through
        bit 7 = S17) follow the upstream source/main.c read_sensors() and the
        raw_S10()..raw_S17() helpers. Added here: polarity and left-to-right
        order normalisation, so callers always see "bit 0 is the leftmost
        sensor, 1 means over the line".

  * docs/hardware.md
        Condensed from the upstream README.md, docs/components.md and
        docs/programming.md.

  * docs/toolchain.md
        Condensed from the upstream docs/programming.md (steps 1, 2, 3).

No upstream images, schematics or PCB files are redistributed here. Follow the
link above for those.

